WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.499 --> 00:00:19.700
I held my breath as Holmes pulled back the curtain and revealed—four suits!

2
00:00:20.761 --> 00:00:23.021
"Oh!" Soames grabbed my arm in relief.

3
00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:25.422
I gave him a reassuring smile.

4
00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:26.903
"Nobody's there!"

5
00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:30.764
Meanwhile Holmes' attention was suddenly drawn to something on the floor.

6
00:00:30.784 --> 00:00:31.864
"What's this?"

7
00:00:32.608 --> 00:00:36.510
The detective picked up a piece of black clay exactly like the one on Soames' desk.

8
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:41.112
"Your visitor seems to have left traces in your bedroom as well as your sitting room."

9
00:00:41.852 --> 00:00:42.712
Soames looked puzzled.

10
00:00:42.732 --> 00:00:44.633
"What could he have wanted in here?"

11
00:00:44.653 --> 00:00:49.255
"When you came back unexpectedly, he gathered up his things and rushed into your bedroom to hide."

12
00:00:49.935 --> 00:00:51.836
Soames' eyes widened in surprise.

13
00:00:51.856 --> 00:00:56.158
"Do you mean that the whole time I was talking to Bannister, the culprit was in here?"

14
00:00:56.178 --> 00:01:00.200
"You had him prisoner, and you didn't even know it."

15
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.222
Holmes rubbed his hands together and strode out of the bedroom.

16
00:01:03.242 --> 00:01:04.322
"Now, Mr.

17
00:01:04.362 --> 00:01:09.086
Soames, if you would be so good as to summon your servant Bannister was a short fellow in

18
00:01:09.126 --> 00:01:12.108
his fifties, who kept taking deep breaths to calm himself.

19
00:01:13.449 --> 00:01:17.171
I wondered if he was still suffering from the shocking disruption of his quiet routine.

20
00:01:17.191 --> 00:01:18.652
"Mr. Holmes and Dr.

21
00:01:18.692 --> 00:01:21.894
Watson are investigating our unhappy discovery," Soames said.

22
00:01:22.495 --> 00:01:26.177
Bannister nodded in our direction but didn't venture very far into the sitting room.

23
00:01:26.197 --> 00:01:29.179
"I understand that you left your key in the door," Holmes said.

24
00:01:29.199 --> 00:01:30.240
"Yes, sir.

25
00:01:30.804 --> 00:01:32.185
I had the tea tray in my hands.

26
00:01:32.806 --> 00:01:35.448
I intended to come back for the key, but then I forgot."

27
00:01:35.468 --> 00:01:38.851
"You were quite upset when you and Mr.

28
00:01:38.911 --> 00:01:41.052
Soames discovered that the proofs had been tampered with?"

29
00:01:42.053 --> 00:01:42.754
"Oh yes, sir.

30
00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:45.276
Nothing like this has ever happened since I've worked here.

31
00:01:45.916 --> 00:01:46.977
I nearly fainted, sir!"

32
00:01:47.778 --> 00:01:48.959
Holmes went on with his questioning.

33
00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:51.281
"And where were you when you started feeling ill?"

34
00:01:52.141 --> 00:01:53.082
"Here, near the door."

35
00:01:53.102 --> 00:01:56.325
"That's odd because you collapsed into the desk chair.

36
00:01:56.845 --> 00:01:59.808
Why did you cross the room to the desk chair when another one was right here?"

37
00:02:00.656 --> 00:02:01.577
"I don't know, sir."

38
00:02:02.478 --> 00:02:03.919
Bannister nervously licked his lips.

39
00:02:03.939 --> 00:02:05.880
"I just needed to sit down."

40
00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.422
Soames was quick to come to Bannister's rescue.

41
00:02:08.442 --> 00:02:10.783
"He really was looking ghastly."

42
00:02:11.484 --> 00:02:13.365
Holmes quizzed the servant for a few more minutes.

43
00:02:13.385 --> 00:02:15.247
"What did you do after Mr.

44
00:02:15.327 --> 00:02:16.488
Soames went in search of me?"

45
00:02:18.289 --> 00:02:21.191
"I sat here for a few minutes, and then I locked the door and went to my room."

46
00:02:21.211 --> 00:02:24.533
"Is there anyone you think might try to cheat on the exam?"

47
00:02:24.914 --> 00:02:25.454
Holmes said.

48
00:02:26.335 --> 00:02:27.816
Bannister shook his head vehemently.

49
00:02:28.668 --> 00:02:31.891
"I can't believe that any young gentleman in this college would try such a thing!"

50
00:02:31.911 --> 00:02:34.673
"One last question," Holmes said.

51
00:02:34.693 --> 00:02:38.216
"Have you mentioned this incident to the three students who live above Mr.

52
00:02:38.296 --> 00:02:41.919
Soames?" Bannister said no, and Holmes dismissed him.

53
00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.020
"Now, Mr.

54
00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:44.681
Soames, let's return to the courtyard."

55
00:02:45.402 --> 00:02:48.805
Holmes headed outside, but I remained with Soames while he locked his door.

56
00:02:49.385 --> 00:02:53.188
When we reached the courtyard, Holmes was looking up at the rooms above Soames' rooms.

57
00:02:53.949 --> 00:02:57.112
It was dark outside now, and lights were on in all three rooms.

58
00:02:59.224 --> 00:03:03.927
"Your three birds are in their nests," Holmes said, "but one of them seems restless."

59
00:03:04.727 --> 00:03:07.529
Daulat Ras' silhouette appeared on his shade, pacing.

60
00:03:07.549 --> 00:03:11.651
"I'd like to talk to each of them without giving away my purpose," Holmes said.

61
00:03:11.671 --> 00:03:12.832
"Is that possible?"

62
00:03:12.852 --> 00:03:14.773
"Yes, it should be easy."

63
00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:17.254
Soames turned to lead us inside.

64
00:03:17.274 --> 00:03:19.775
"These rooms are some of the oldest in the college.

65
00:03:20.496 --> 00:03:22.417
It's not unusual for visitors to want to see them."

66
00:03:23.137 --> 00:03:26.479
Soames was about to knock on Richard Gilchrist's door when Holmes cautioned him.

67
00:03:27.259 --> 00:03:27.960
"No names, please.

68
00:03:28.616 --> 00:03:30.156
I don't want anyone to know who I am."

69
00:03:30.857 --> 00:03:33.557
After Soames knocked, a tall, blond student let us in.

70
00:03:34.198 --> 00:03:39.499
The room did contain some interesting architectural details, and Holmes was particularly delighted by the fireplace.

71
00:03:41.119 --> 00:03:44.300
He was in the midst of sketching it in his notebook when his pencil broke.

72
00:03:45.241 --> 00:03:49.942
After borrowing a pencil from Gilchrist, he resumed sketching and then borrowed a knife to sharpen his own

73
00:03:49.982 --> 00:03:52.743
pencil. The same thing happened in Ras' room.

74
00:03:53.523 --> 00:03:57.104
The student eyed us skeptically but produced a pencil and a knife for Holmes to use.

75
00:03:58.056 --> 00:04:00.737
Miles McLaren was the only student who refused to let us in.

76
00:04:00.757 --> 00:04:02.457
"I don't care who you are!"

77
00:04:02.917 --> 00:04:04.138
he shouted through his closed door.

78
00:04:04.158 --> 00:04:05.398
"Go away!

79
00:04:05.838 --> 00:04:07.239
I'm studying for an important exam."

80
00:04:07.979 --> 00:04:08.879
"What a rude fellow!"

81
00:04:09.699 --> 00:04:11.720
Soames huffed and led us back downstairs.

82
00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:16.801
"Of course, he didn't realize I was at the door too, but his behavior was disrespectful and suspicious."

83
00:04:17.542 --> 00:04:19.902
I found Holmes' next question to be rather strange.

84
00:04:21.523 --> 00:04:23.763
He asked Soames how tall McLaren was.

85
00:04:24.423 --> 00:04:24.924
"Really, Mr.

86
00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.124
Holmes, I have no idea."

87
00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:28.413
Soames seemed impatient and annoyed.

88
00:04:28.433 --> 00:04:31.495
"I would say he's taller than Ras but shorter than Gilchrist."

89
00:04:31.995 --> 00:04:33.976
"That could be important," Holmes said.

90
00:04:33.996 --> 00:04:35.457
"And now I wish you good night."

91
00:04:35.477 --> 00:04:38.299
"What?" Soames uttered a cry of dismay.

92
00:04:38.319 --> 00:04:40.420
"Surely you're not going to leave me now!

93
00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.301
You don't seem to understand the position I'm in.

94
00:04:43.962 --> 00:04:47.564
If you don't find the culprit soon, I can't allow the exam to take place tomorrow."

95
00:04:48.164 --> 00:04:49.225
Holmes tried to soothe him.

96
00:04:49.245 --> 00:04:51.626
"There's no need to take any action tonight.

97
00:04:52.387 --> 00:04:54.568
Finish reading your proofs and send them to the printer.

98
00:04:55.224 --> 00:04:58.927
When I return first thing tomorrow, I hope to be able to straighten everything out."

99
00:04:58.947 --> 00:05:01.509
"Hope?" Soames cried.

100
00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.472
From the look on his face, Soames was obviously not soothed.

101
00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:12.417
But Holmes left the teacher's rooms anyway, taking the two pieces of black clay, the pencil shavings, and

102
00:05:12.457 --> 00:05:13.137
the broken lead.

103
00:05:13.758 --> 00:05:16.840
As we went through the college gates, Holmes asked my opinion on the case.

104
00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:22.224
"I'd say McLaren is guilty because he wouldn't let us in, but Ras was acting suspiciously too.

105
00:05:22.944 --> 00:05:25.966
Why was he pacing across his room if he wasn't anxious about something?"

106
00:05:25.986 --> 00:05:29.469
"Many people do that when they're trying to memorize something," Holmes said.

107
00:05:29.489 --> 00:05:31.990
"Yes, but he looked annoyed when we met him."

108
00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:36.573
"You'd look annoyed too, Watson, if two strangers invaded your room while you were preparing for an important

109
00:05:36.593 --> 00:05:38.895
exam. No, I don't have a problem with that.

110
00:05:39.415 --> 00:05:41.857
And there was nothing strange about the students' pencils and knives.

111
00:05:41.877 --> 00:05:44.879
"But Bannister puzzles me.

112
00:05:45.479 --> 00:05:46.320
What's he up to?"

113
00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.022
"He seemed honest to me," I said.

114
00:05:49.042 --> 00:05:51.864
"Exactly," Holmes said as we crossed the street.

115
00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.861
"So, why would an honest man—oh, never mind.

116
00:05:55.542 --> 00:05:56.963
Let's go into this stationery store.

117
00:05:57.463 --> 00:05:59.764
Luckily, the shops stay open late in this college town."

118
00:06:00.384 --> 00:06:04.447
At each of our four stationery stores, Holmes showed his pencil shavings to a clerk.

119
00:06:05.087 --> 00:06:09.770
The clerks all recognized the Faber brand, but none remembered selling the unusual blue pencil.

120
00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.011
Back on the street, Holmes sighed.

121
00:06:12.031 --> 00:06:15.633
"That wasn't very helpful, but I think I know who the cheater is."

122
00:06:16.653 --> 00:06:21.316
"Who?" At this point I was desperately hungry for supper and wanted a break from this case.

123
00:06:21.816 --> 00:06:22.937
"Patience, my dear Watson."

124
00:06:23.578 --> 00:06:24.499
Holmes smiled at me.

125
00:06:24.519 --> 00:06:28.664
"All will be revealed tomorrow—after I check one final detail."
